            <ArticleTitle>Changing the dehydrogenation pathway of LiBH4-MgH2via nanosized lithiated TiO2.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7455-7460</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cp08278e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nanosized lithiated titanium oxide (LixTiO2) noticeably improves the kinetic behaviour of 2LiBH4 + MgH2. The presence of LixTiO2 reduces the time required for the first dehydrogenation by suppressing the intermediate reaction to Li2B12H12, leading to direct MgB2 formation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
